    },
    "body": "This drops the `WITH_VALGRIND: 'no'` and `CTIMETESTS: 'no'` overrides from the arm64-debian job. They are left over from when the job ran under QEMU. Without them, the job runs `ctime_tests` under Valgrind for gcc, clang and both snapshots, as theStack suggested in #1975.\n\nI ran `ci/ci.sh` with the job's settings on aarch64 (Debian trixie, Valgrind 3.24) with gcc 14.2 and clang 19.1. `ctime_tests` passes with both. It fails with both after I plant a secret-dependent branch in `secp256k1_ecdsa_sig_sign`.\n",
